{"overview":"A group of New York society folk on a yachting excursion are forced to put into a New England fishing village for repairs. The engaged couple Reggie and Patricia are taken with the quaint town and its quainter ways, but also with two locals, Betty Alden and her brother John. Patricia begins to fall for John while her fiancé takes a seemingly unworthy liking to Betty. The new infatuations lead to disharmony.","cast":[{"n":"Richard Barthelmess","c":"John Alden Jr.","p":"/p7nmZeuQjHOsNFgqgEXBdh78OSC.jpg","q":"Q457293"},{"n":"Frank Losee","c":"Uncle Jim Alden","p":"/360fNiKoqVmkDgDki3lGUfVdTfn.jpg","q":"Q15177567"},{"n":"Leslie Stowe","c":"Uncle Ned","p":"/epc1WcsAZirIspdongHO6tYHFS.jpg","q":"Q81780683"},{"n":"Tammany Young","c":"Donald Peabody","p":"/r0ger3ri1mCYz4UlZvb9fi8gTLl.jpg","q":"Q7681531"},{"n":"George Stewart","c":"Reggie Van Zandt","p":"/4nnFJ2KxttO5G1F6aZwHU9cLMGr.jpg","q":"Q67524228"},{"n":"Alfred Schmid","c":"Monty Pell","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Grace Barton","c":"Aunt Abigail","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Anne Cornwall","c":"Betty Alden","p":"/1hcYpIwOk5WP1BlebBipkXp1RMv.jpg","q":"Q3617936"},{"n":"Patterson Dial","c":"Katinka","p":"/uBpk5a5CCrUcuGKzWGfVcImSG6m.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Teddie Gerard","c":"'Billie' Blair","p":"/qqQdVyVjn8v93hVu3UtFlVLEJJY.jpg","q":null}],"country":["United States"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Seventh_Day_(1922_film)","qid":"Q2678834","rel":{"US":{"d":"1922-02-06"}},"stills":["silent-the-seventh-day_1.webp","silent-the-seventh-day_2.webp","silent-the-seventh-day_3.webp","silent-the-seventh-day_4.webp"]}